[2025-10-20T18:21:26Z INFO  ai_agent_audit::llm_review::phases::add_poc_findings] AI Agent: This PoC demonstrates the O(n²) gas complexity vulnerability in PuppyRaffle's enterRaffle function. The test adds 100 unique addresses to the players array, measures gas usage, then adds 100 more and measures again to show the quadratic growth in gas consumption. The test proves that gas usage grows more than linearly (more than 2x when doubling players), and calculates that with 1000 players, the gas would exceed Ethereum's block gas limit (~30M), making the contract unusable. This allows an attacker to permanently DoS the raffle by bloating the players array with unique addresses.
